      "text": "Four questions worth being able to answer with a screenshot this week. First: does every outbound message path - including VIP one-to-one texts and any third-party tool - traverse a hard exclusion gate, and can you reconstruct two years of outbound contact by exclusion status on demand? Colorado required exactly that of Fanatics. Second: can your PAM express product entitlement and jurisdictional partitioning as configuration rather than code? Fanatics now runs sportsbook, casino and CFTC event contracts on one balance with the visible product set resolved by location at session level, and DraftKings and Betr are on the same path. Third: which financial signal drives your affordability model - net deposits and withdrawals, or turnover-derived stakes minus winnings? Sweden may force the answer, and the false-positive volumes differ by an order of magnitude. Fourth: how much of your product catalogue arrives on day one of a new market versus six months later? bet365 shipped Jackpot365 and Early Payout Offer into West Virginia at launch, its sixth North American entry in 13 months, which is a configuration benchmark rather than a marketing one. Also worth a look: bet builders hit 22% of live bets at the 2026 World Cup against 3% in 2022, which argues for correlated-market pricing and settlement latency over pre-match market breadth.",
