    "section": "North America",
    "title": "Fanatics launches single app merging sportsbook, online casino and prediction markets on one FanCash wallet",
    "meta": "Legal Sports Report | 2 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "Fanatics has launched Fanatics Sports & Casino, a unified app giving customers one login and one FanCash balance across its sportsbook (live in 23 states plus Washington DC), its online casino (Michigan, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and West Virginia) and Fanatics Markets, its CFTC-regulated event contracts platform offered in 22 states and four US territories. The app auto-detects a customer's location and adjusts which verticals are available, and folds in the Fanatics ONE loyalty programme. It makes Fanatics the third US operator after DraftKings and Betr to ship a genuine multi-vertical super app.",
    "why": "This is the clearest US signal yet that the single-wallet, single-account, geo-aware product stack is now table stakes rather than a differentiator. The hard part is not the front end but the platform underneath: one KYC and account record, one balance that has to be legally partitioned by vertical and jurisdiction, and a rules engine that decides at session level which products a given user may even see. Loyalty is the tell here, because FanCash spanning betting, casino and event contracts requires a unified player-value model across three different regulatory regimes and three different margin profiles. For B2B platform vendors the question becomes whether a PAM can express product entitlement as configuration rather than code, because operators will otherwise build this themselves. Anyone selling into North America should expect entitlement-by-geolocation and cross-vertical bonus wallets to appear in the next round of RFPs.",
    "expanded": "Fanatics Betting and Gaming has consolidated three previously separate products into one app, Fanatics Sports & Casino, launched on 2 September 2026 ahead of the NFL season. The single account covers sportsbook in 23 states plus Washington DC, online casino in Michigan, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and West Virginia, and Fanatics Markets event contracts in 22 states and four US territories. The app detects a customer's location and adjusts the available product set accordingly, so the experience changes by state. CEO Matt King said: 'Sports fans have been asking for a better gaming experience, and this is it. Fanatics Sports & Casino gives fans across America one app where the experience travels with them, from betting the game, to trading on its biggest moments, to playing casino games.' King added: 'And because it's Fanatics, every one of those bets, trades or plays earns FanCash; we can uniquely connect what fans play to what fans love in one ecosystem.' FanCash can be redeemed against merchandise, tickets and collectibles, and the Fanatics ONE loyalty tier structure is embedded in the app. The launch caps a busy period: Fanatics became one of the NFL's official sports betting and online casino partners, and in July acquired Water Street Labs so that Fanatics Markets owns its own exchange and clearinghouse. DraftKings shipped its Super App in March, linking sportsbook, casino, predictions and lottery, while Betr is building a comparable stack around a Polymarket prediction market partnership.",
