    "meta": "SBC Americas | 27 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "bet365 launched online sports betting and iGaming in West Virginia on 27 August 2026, making the state its 18th US online sports betting jurisdiction and the fourth in which it also runs online casino. The operator received an interim licence in January and full annual approval on 29 July, and brought across its Early Payout Offer plus the newly launched Jackpot365 multi-tier progressive feature. West Virginia now hosts 10 online sports wagering licensees, and the launch is bet365's sixth North American market entry in 13 months after Kansas, Maryland, Missouri, Michigan and Alberta.",
    "why": "bet365's cadence of roughly one new North American market every two months is a case study in how much of regulated market entry is now repeatable configuration rather than fresh build. The interesting detail is Jackpot365 shipping into a new state at launch rather than as a later phase, which implies the jackpot engine and its state-sealed pooling are already parameterised for new jurisdictions. Early Payout Offer travelling intact matters too, because automated cash-out and settlement rules are exactly the sort of logic that usually gets re-scoped per regulator. For anyone competing on platform, the benchmark is no longer whether you can enter a state but how much of the product catalogue arrives on day one versus six months later. West Virginia's ten licensees also underline how crowded small iGaming states have become, which pushes differentiation back onto product depth and cashier quality.",
    "expanded": "bet365 opened for business in West Virginia on Thursday 27 August 2026, in time for the college football and NFL seasons, for customers aged 21 and over. Per West Virginia Lottery licensing documents the operator held an interim licence from January and was approved for a full annual licence on 29 July. West Virginia is bet365's 18th US online sports betting state and the fourth where it also offers online casino. Trip Stoddard, bet365 Head of Development, said: 'West Virginia represents another important step in bet365's continued expansion across North America. As we grow our presence across the region, our focus remains on bringing customers the quality, depth and functionality that define the bet365 platform. With football season just around the corner, it's an exciting time to introduce our sportsbook and casino offerings to customers across the state.' Features included at launch are the Early Payout Offer, which settles qualifying bets as winners when a football team takes a 17-point lead, and Jackpot365, a multi-tier progressive jackpot integrated directly within a betslip or casino game. The state now has 10 online sports wagering operator licensees: bet365, BetRivers, BetMGM, Caesars, DraftKings, Ember Casino & Sportsbook, Fanatics, FanDuel, Kambi and theScore Bet, with several running multiple casino brands including PENN's Hollywood Casino, Caesars' Horseshoe Casino and DraftKings-owned Golden Nugget Online Gaming. West Virginia follows Kansas and Maryland in August 2025, Missouri in December 2025, Michigan in April 2026 and Alberta in July 2026. bet365 spent around $135m on a 120,000 square foot Denver headquarters. The Massachusetts Gaming Commission voted unanimously in April to reopen its sports betting application process after a written request from bet365, which declined to comment on whether it will apply.",
