    "section": "Product",
    "title": "Kambi rebrands around AI and network scale as bet builder share hits 22% of live bets",
    "meta": "SBC News | 2 Sep 2026",
    "summary": "Kambi has launched a new brand identity and strategic positioning, 'Powerful Network. Proven Edge.', folding Tzeract's AI trading platform, Shape Games' frontend technology and the Abios esports business under a single Kambi brand. The identity is built around a network of over 70 partners in more than 100 regulated markets, around EUR 17bn of annual turnover and 1.5 billion bets. Kambi says its AI platform traded the entire 2026 World Cup at an 18% operator trading margin, with bet builders accounting for 22% of live bets during the tournament versus 3% in 2022.",
    "why": "The interesting part is not the logo but the collapsing of three separately-marketed assets into one commercial proposition - that changes how a sportsbook supplier is bought. Operators evaluating Kambi now buy trading, frontend and esports as a bundled stack rather than picking components, which raises the switching cost and narrows the room for a best-of-breed frontend on top of someone else's odds feed. The 3% to 22% jump in bet builder share of live bets is the number to take into roadmap conversations: it is a direct argument for prioritising correlated-market pricing, settlement latency and bet builder UX over breadth of pre-match markets. An 18% trading margin claimed on fully AI-traded World Cup markets also sets a benchmark that in-house and rival trading teams will be measured against.",
    "expanded": "Kambi Group has unveiled a refreshed brand and positioning under the strategic promise 'Powerful Network. Proven Edge.', reported by SBC News on 2 September 2026. The refresh unifies capabilities that had been marketed under separate names: Tzeract, Kambi's AI trading platform; Shape Games, its frontend and app technology; and Abios, its esports data and betting business. All now sit under a single Kambi identity. The supporting numbers are the substance of the announcement: more than 70 partners live across more than 100 regulated markets, roughly EUR 17bn in annual turnover flowing through the network and approximately 1.5 billion bets handled. Kambi says the AI platform traded the whole of the 2026 World Cup and delivered an 18% operator trading margin across the tournament. Bet builder products made up 22% of live bets during the 2026 World Cup, compared with 3% at the 2022 edition - a sevenfold shift in only one World Cup cycle. Kambi's stated direction is that AI will let it price and trade a wider range of betting opportunities while making sportsbook experiences more dynamic and personalised. The rebrand lands weeks before SBC Summit Lisbon (29 September to 1 October) and follows Kambi's August 2026 ten-year turnkey sportsbook and PAM deal with Station Casinos, its first entry into Nevada. Watch for whether the unified brand is followed by unified commercial terms, and whether Tzeract remains sellable as a standalone trading layer to operators running someone else's frontend.",
